    {
      "date": "2026-10-04",
      "category": "Backend",
      "title": "stabilise MongoDB connection startup and DNS fallback (Issue #20)",
      "description": "Stabilised the MongoDB connection and its DNS fallback (config/db.ts, config/env.ts, server.ts). The fallback stays: on a mongodb+srv:// URI whose resolver refuses SRV queries (querySrv ECONNREFUSED) connectDB retries once with public resolvers (MONGO_DNS_SERVERS, default 8.8.8.8,1.1.1.1). New: (1) getMongoConfig() validates MONGO_URI (scheme), MONGO_DNS_SERVERS (literal IPs, ip:port, [ipv6]:port; previously a bad entry threw ERR_INVALID_IP_ADDRESS only after the first connection failed, hiding the real error) and the new MONGO_SERVER_SELECTION_TIMEOUT_MS (1000-120000, default 15000 instead of the driver's implicit 30000 per attempt) before any DNS/network work, at startup in server.ts and again in connectDB; error messages never contain MONGO_URI or its credentials (the timeout and DNS-server errors do quote the offending value, a number or IP-shaped string). MONGO_DNS_SERVERS: unset, empty and whitespace-only all mean defaults; only a separator with no entries (',' or ' , ') disables the fallback (before, a whitespace-only value silently disabled it). (2) connectDB is single-flight: concurrent callers share one attempt, an already-connected call is a no-op, a settled attempt clears the slot. A probe against real Mongoose 9.4.1 showed two overlapping calls where one logged 'MongoDB connected' at readyState 0, and the DNS save/restore could capture the fallback servers as the originals; neither can happen now. Success is confirmed from readyState === 1. (3) The process-wide dns.setServers() override is applied for the single fallback attempt only, restored in finally on success/failure/throw (a failed restore is logged CRITICAL and never replaces the real error) and is documented in code and docs/context.md so it is not 'cleaned up'. (4) Logging names only the path (SRV, direct, SRV via fallback DNS), the timeout and an error's name/code; never the URI, host, user or password. Unchanged: fallback trigger condition, default servers, no retry loop, Mongoose buffering defaults, error propagation to exitWithFatalError. Tests: tests/mongoConfig.test.ts and tests/mongoConnection.test.ts (70, injected driver/resolver doubles plus one test against the real node:dns state; no Atlas, DNS or network). 27 mutants (restore removed, previous captured late, no single-flight, in-flight not cleared, no/changed timeout, each fallback condition, no readyState check, URI/host leaked in logs, restore error swallowed or replacing the real error, each validation bound, whitespace-only handling) were caught. Known limits: tests/api.routes.test.ts still needs MongoMemoryServer (download blocked in the sandbox) and was not run; a real Atlas connection and a real refused-SRV resolver were not exercised (the connect path was probed against a refusing local resolver only); server.ts is not unit-testable (runs on import); the driver's sharded-topology SRV polling would use the platform resolver after the override is restored; the final fatal log still prints the driver error object. Not done on purpose: connection event handlers, a retry framework, a private dns.Resolver.",
