    {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "category": "Bugfix",
      "title": "3009: move AI task creation behind the authenticated backend (Issue #22)",
      "description": "The browser called Groq directly with a Bearer key read from import.meta.env.VITE_GROQ_API_KEY, so the secret was shipped in the client bundle. AI parsing now goes through POST /api/ai/parse-tasks behind the existing requireAuth middleware. Request: { prompt } (non-empty after trimming, max 2000 chars; any provider/model/url/temperature fields are ignored because provider, model, endpoint and max_tokens are server constants). Response: 200 { tasks: [{ title, priority, dueDate?, estimatedMinutes?, tags, description }] }; the server runs the same parsing prompt and sanitises the model output (max 20 tasks, bounded title/description/tags, real YYYY-MM-DD dates, valid minutes), and the client keeps its draft mapping so the UX is unchanged. Validation runs before any provider call. Errors are generic: 400 invalid, 429 provider rate-limited, 502 provider unavailable/auth failure/bad output (a provider 401/403 is never forwarded as 401, which would log the user out), 504 timeout (20s), 503 GROQ_API_KEY not configured; provider text, the key, prompts and generated content are never returned or logged. The key lives only in the server-only GROQ_API_KEY (config/env.ts getGroqApiKey; documented in server .env.example, .env.production and README; server.ts warns when unset). VITE_GROQ_API_KEY was removed from client code and env files, and the client production bundle was scanned and contains no provider reference. Rate limiting: no reusable limiter exists; per the issue none was built, the endpoint is bounded by auth, prompt cap, max_tokens and timeout, and per-user limiting depends on Issue #23. Tests: 41 new server tests (39 in aiRoutes.test.ts with fetch mocked, 2 in env.test.ts) and 16 new client tests (aiService, hook, and a source scan that fails if a provider reference or key variable reappears). Known limits: tests/api.routes.test.ts still needs MongoMemoryServer, which cannot download its binary in the sandbox; no per-user rate limit until Issue #23; the prompt's 'today' is the server UTC date, as the browser's was.",
